+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house in South Carolina while living out of state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You sign the deed before a notary in your own state, with two witnesses, and it records in Horry County as if you had signed it here. A person you name with a power of attorney can also sign for you."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to be at the closing?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Every home closing here must be supervised by a South Carolina attorney, whose office records the deed in Conway and sends you your money after the closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the South Carolina nonresident withholding?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When the seller's permanent home is outside South Carolina, the buyer must hold back part of the price for state income tax, unless the sale is exempt. With the seller's affidavit, Form I-295, the hold-back is figured on the gain instead of the whole price."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do out-of-state buyers pay more?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No sign of it. In the same building or subdivision, buyers with an out-of-state tax bill paid the same middle price as South Carolina buyers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many people move to Myrtle Beach a year?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 14,200 more people moved into Horry County from the rest of the United States than moved out in the year to July 2025, about 39 a day."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is fall a bad time to sell to out-of-state buyers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Out-of-state buyers closed every month. October had the most closings, 352, and January the fewest, 207."}}]}</script>
