+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/sell/">Sell</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Out-of-State Buyers</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Selling</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Who buys Grand Strand homes from out of state,<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">and how to sell yours from far away.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated June 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Our count of a year of Horry County deeds, the law for signing from another state, and what South Carolina holds back at closing.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 10 homes sold in Horry County in the year to September 2026 went to a buyer whose tax bill goes to another state. For condos it was more than half. In the same building or subdivision, those buyers paid the same middle price as South Carolina buyers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you live in another state, you can sell without coming back. You sign the deed before a notary where you live, with two witnesses, and it records in Horry County as if you had signed it here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Live in another state? Get a price and a closing plan for your home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/sell/#seller-cma-form">Get my price and plan</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#who-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who buys</a></li><li><a href="#pay-more" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do they pay more</a></li><li><a href="#where-from" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where they come from</a></li><li><a href="#when" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">When they buy</a></li><li><a href="#sell-from-away" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Selling from away</a></li><li><a href="#withholding" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What the state holds back</a></li><li><a href="#disclosure" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your disclosure</a></li><li><a href="#selling-from-out-of-state-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em